					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-10-30 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br><p style="font: normal normal normal 10px/normal &#39;Lucida Grande&#39;; margin: 0px">When <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">KEXP&#39;s Darek Mazzone </span>aint playing world music on Tuesday nights, he&#39;s interviewing producers and musicians for <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Crossfader.com</span>. Here&#39;s a three part video interview he did with your boy <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Sabzi </span>(who is competing in the<span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">&nbsp;Big Tune </span>beat battle national finals this Thursday at Neumo&#39;s in Seattle!).</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 10px/normal &#39;Lucida Grande&#39;; margin: 0px">&nbsp;</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 10px/normal &#39;Lucida Grande&#39;; margin: 0px"><object width="425" height="355"><param name="movie" value="http://www.youtube.com/v/kDPQCunPUR4&amp;rel=1"></param><param name="wmode" value="transparent"></param></object></p><p style="font: normal normal normal 10px/normal &#39;Lucida Grande&#39;; margin: 0px"><object width="425" height="355"><param name="movie" value="http://www.youtube.com/v/IuB1XAMmZRs&amp;rel=1"></param><param name="wmode" value="transparent"></param></object></p><p style="font: normal normal normal 10px/normal &#39;Lucida Grande&#39;; margin: 0px"><object width="425" height="355"><param name="movie" value="http://www.youtube.com/v/r2rv5PJLsoM&amp;rel=1"></param><param name="wmode" value="transparent"></param></object></p><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-10-26 | Friday</font></strong><br><br>Macklemore<div>Scribes</div><div>Chev</div><div>The Knowmads</div><div>BYC Break Group</div><div>Language Arts</div><div>B Awake</div><div>DJ Roscoe</div><div><br /></div><div>Hosted by Khingz of Abyssinian Creole</div><div><br /></div><div>$6 @ THE VERA PROJECT (730PM)</div><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-10-26 | Friday</font></strong><br><br><img src="http://farm3.static.flickr.com/2194/1761658609_a05ba641f1_o.jpg" alt="" width="430" height="323" /><br /><em><br />COMMONmarket, Photo courtesy of M.</em><br /><br />Peace<br />daps1<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-10-24 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Myriad Pro; margin: 0px"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 10px" class="Apple-style-span">The fifth and final day of <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">DV One&#39;s</span> trial goes down today (Wed, 10/24). <span style="font-weight: bold" class="Apple-style-span">Julie C</span> gets props over here for the <a href="../smf/index.php?topic=3450.0">timely and thorough reports which you can read here</a>. Closing arguments begin at 9am at the King County Courthouse. Peace to all the working people who can&#39;t be there but stand in solidarity. Everybody else - no excuses! Be there!</span></p><div><br /></div><div>King County Superior Court&nbsp;</div><div>516 3rd Ave&nbsp;</div><div>Courtroom W-817</div><div>Wednesday, October 24, 2007 9am</div><div><br /></div><div>From <a href="http://www.myspace.com/supportdvone">Myspace.com/supportdvone</a>:</div><blockquote><span style="font-family: Myriad Pro; font-size: 12px" class="Apple-style-span"><span style="font-style: italic" class="Apple-style-span">IMPORTANT NOTE:&nbsp;</span></span><span style="font-style: italic" class="Apple-style-span"><br /></span><span style="font-family: Myriad Pro; font-size: 12px" class="Apple-style-span"><span style="font-style: italic" class="Apple-style-span">Spectators should be aware that Judge Canova is not likely to allow any audible expression of hostility toward the prosecution witnesses or support for Toby, and that sort of thing can alienate jurors. People can subtly show their affection for Toby though. The jurors will understand whom they are there to support.&nbsp;</span></span><span style="font-style: italic" class="Apple-style-span"><br /><br /></span><span style="font-family: Myriad Pro; font-size: 12px" class="Apple-style-span"><span style="font-style: italic" class="Apple-style-span">On behalf of DV One, &quot;Thank you for your support and well wishes throughout this ordeal. It is greatly appreciated.&quot;&nbsp;</span></span><span style="font-style: italic" class="Apple-style-span"><br /><br /></span><span style="font-family: Myriad Pro; font-size: 12px" class="Apple-style-span"><span style="font-style: italic" class="Apple-style-span">Please continue to come back to check for details as they become available.&nbsp;</span></span></blockquote><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-10-23 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br><div align="center"><strong>Yo! Check out the aforementioned Blue Scholars video at </strong><br /><br /><strong><a href="thenewpop.com">thenewpop.com</a><br /><br /><br />Also check out the new midwest tour dates on your right. Blue Scholars in ya area soon!<br /><br /></strong><div align="left"><br />Peace<br />daps1<br /></div></div><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> [12] <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=140">[29]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[31]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[32]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=170">[35]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=175">[36]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=180">[37]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=185">[38]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=190">[39]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=195">[40]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=200">[41]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=205">[42]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=210">[43]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=215">[44]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=220">[45]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=225">[46]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=230">[47]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=235">[48]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=240">[49]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=245">[50]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=250">[51]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=255">[52]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=260">[53]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=265">[54]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=270">[55]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=275">